  "notes": "Source: official Benedict College 'Programs of Study 2023-2024' (benedict.edu), PROGRAM OF STUDY IN BIOLOGY (School of Science and Engineering), transcribed verbatim 2026-10-01 from a fresh re-read of the PDF. Published semester subtotals (17/14/15/17/15/14/14/14) reconcile exactly to Total SCH 120. 'STEM 230/SCI 230', 'CSC 230/STEM 233/Math 236', 'FR/SP/AR 233', and 'SCI 331 or Honors 340' are catalog 'X or Y' choices (code = first-listed option). NOTE: the PDF text extraction renders the Junior-year CHEM 237 row as 'Organic Chemistry II'; the same document's Chemistry program defines CHEM 237 as Organic Chemistry I (paired with CHEM 217L Organic Chemistry I Lab), so the same-document course title is used and the discrepancy is documented here. 'BIO 200/300/400 Level', 'BIO Elective', 'Minor/Elective', 'Elective', and 'Global & Intercultural Learning' entries are catalog placeholders recorded as choice slots. Degree designation B.S. in Biology per benedict.edu/schools-majors/. The plan prints no prerequisite chains; prereq arrays left empty rather than invented.",
